---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<SiteLayout title="Interactive engineering portfolio" description="Ruslan AI Lab: practical interactive web experiments, transparent AI-assisted engineering, original source and verifiable case studies.">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-led" aria-hidden="true"></span> INDEPENDENT ENGINEERING WORKBENCH / 2026</p>
        <h1>Engineering you can <em>try</em> — and verify.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">Small, practical web experiments. Readable source code. Tests you can inspect. A transparent, AI-assisted approach to building on the web.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={base + "labs/css-studio/"}>Try CSS Studio <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai/ruslan-ai-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <p class="fine-print">No sign-up · No tracking · No paid integrations</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-graphic" role="img" aria-label="Original abstract engineering layout illustration made from CSS grid shapes">
        <div class="diagram-top"><span>FIG. 001 / SYSTEM DESIGN</span><span>STATIC / NO WEBGL</span></div>
        <div class="diagram-grid" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="diagram-block diagram-block-a"><span>01</span></div>
          <div class="diagram-block diagram-block-b"><span>02</span></div>
          <div class="diagram-block diagram-block-c"><span>03</span></div>
          <div class="diagram-block diagram-block-d"><span>04</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="diagram-bottom">CONSTRAINTS <span>→</span> IMPLEMENTATION <span>→</span> EVIDENCE</div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="section-separator"><span>001 / INTERACTIVE LAB</span><span>USE IT. INSPECT IT.</span></div>
    <section class="home-feature" aria-labelledby="lab-heading">
      <div class="feature-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">FEATURED WORKING EXPERIMENT</p><h2 id="lab-heading">CSS Studio <span class="heading-accent">/</span></h2></div><p>Adjust design tokens, see the result immediately, and take the generated CSS with you. No sandbox backend or hidden API.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-abstract" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="abstract-card"><div class="abstract-stripe"></div><div class="abstract-copy"></div><div class="abstract-copy short"></div><div class="abstract-buttons"><span></span><span></span></div></div>
          <div class="abstract-controls"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-detail"><span class="lab-number">LAB / 001</span><h3>From token to interface.</h3><p>Five bounded controls. Deterministic output. Keyboard-friendly native inputs. Built as a real, inspectable client-side experiment.</p><a href={base + "labs/css-studio/"} class="text-link">Open the working lab <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="section-separator"><span>002 / PROOF OVER PROMISES</span><span>REAL SOURCE. REAL HISTORY.</span></div>
    <section class="evidence-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-heading">
      <div class="feature-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING CASE STUDIES</p><h2 id="evidence-heading">The work behind<br />the work.</h2></div><p>What changed, why it changed, what the tests show — and what still needs independent verification.</p></div>
      <article class="case-row"><div class="case-symbol" aria-hidden="true">O<span>1</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">CASE 001 / ASTRO INTEGRATION</p><h3>Opalubka</h3><p>A separate static demo that moved from a legacy HTML concept toward tested Astro. Includes review history, licensing decisions, and a real GitHub Pages build issue.</p></div><a class="case-open" href={base + "case-studies/opalubka/"} >Read Opalubka case ↗</a></article>
      <article class="case-row"><div class="case-symbol" aria-hidden="true">W<span>2</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">CASE 002 / VISUAL REGRESSION</p><h3>When green CI missed a black WebGL frame</h3><p>Screenshot review caught a paused 3D scene rendering black in simulated mobile WebKit. Follow the renderer fix, new framebuffer assertion and repeatable checks.</p></div><a class="case-open" href={base + "case-studies/webkit-frame/"}>Read WebKit case ↗</a></article>
      <article class="case-row"><div class="case-symbol" aria-hidden="true">R<span>3</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">CASE 003 / RELEASE GOVERNANCE</p><h3>Five labs, one human-controlled release</h3><p>From scope and reviewable PRs to source-pinned automated tests, an explicit owner decision and a real Pages deployment.</p></div><a class="case-open" href={base + "case-studies/release-gates/"}>Read release case ↗</a></article>
    </section>
    <p class="project-index-invite"><a class="text-link" href={base + "projects/"}>Explore verified public projects ↗</a></p>
    <div class="section-separator"><span>003 / ENGINEERING METHOD</span><span>DECISIONS BEFORE DEMOS.</span></div>
    <section class="method-section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A TRANSPARENT AI-ASSISTED PROCESS</p>
          <h2 id="method-heading">How the work gets verified.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The owner sets goals, constraints and release decisions. AI tools can help implement, test and review. Public records show what was checked, not who typed every line.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="professional-summary" aria-label="Engineering approach and public contact"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE WORK / AI-ASSISTED DELIVERY</p><p>I define scope, coordinate AI-assisted implementation and review the evidence before approving integration or release. This portfolio shows native web experiments, reproducible tests and candid records of bugs and fixes—not claims of autonomous production AI.</p><a href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See the public GitHub profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <ol class="method-grid">
        <li class="method-card">
          <span class="method-index" aria-hidden="true">01 / SCOPE</span>
          <h3>Define the boundary.</h3>
          <p>Start with a real problem, acceptance criteria and explicit limits. Decide what should not be built or published yet.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai/ruslan-ai-lab/pull/1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Read the P0 specification (opens in a new tab)">Read the P0 specification <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </li>
        <li class="method-card">
          <span class="method-index" aria-hidden="true">02 / IMPLEMENT</span>
          <h3>Build and test.</h3>
          <p>Use small, reproducible changes and deterministic tests. Automated checks report a specific source revision, not permanent quality.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai/ruslan-ai-lab/actions/runs/41176807380" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Inspect a real CI run (opens in a new tab)">Inspect a real CI run <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </li>
        <li class="method-card">
          <span class="method-index" aria-hidden="true">03 / REVIEW</span>
          <h3>Accept with evidence.</h3>
          <p>Compare code, screenshots and known limitations. The owner decides on integration and release separately from automated test results.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai/ruslan-ai-lab/pull/2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Follow the reviewed MVP (opens in a new tab)">Follow the reviewed MVP <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="method-disclaimer">These are links to historical GitHub records, not a connected agent dashboard. This lab does not run an AI agent or monitor repository activity in real time.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="section-separator"><span>004 / OTHER LABS</span><span>FOUR WORKING LABS</span></div>
    <section class="planned-section" aria-labelledby="next-heading"><h2 id="next-heading">Explore more experiments.</h2><div class="planned-grid">
      <article class="planned-card"><span class="planned-index">02 / WORKING LAB</span><h3>Canvas Lab</h3><p>Play, pause and reset a seeded particle field. No backend, WebGL or hidden API.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + "labs/canvas/"}>Try Canvas Lab <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      <article class="planned-card"><span class="planned-index">03 / WORKING LAB</span><h3>3D Playground</h3><p>Opt in to a native WebGL cube and adjust material, light and camera. Static fallback is available without GPU support.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + "labs/3d/"}>Try 3D Playground <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      <article class="planned-card"><span class="planned-index">04 / WORKING LAB</span><h3>AI Workflow Simulator</h3><p>Step through a clearly labeled local simulation of an issue, agent draft, PR, CI, owner review and release decision.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + "labs/workflow/"}>Try Workflow Simulator <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      <article class="planned-card"><span class="planned-index">05 / WORKING LAB</span><h3>Browser APIs Lab</h3><p>Reorder a fixed workflow with accessible controls or pointer drag. Save it in your browser only when you choose.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + "labs/browser-apis/"}>Try Browser APIs Lab <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
    </div></section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
